# Fixed passive runtime-inventory acquisition

This getter admits only the exact 211,161-byte `requests.json` manifest with SHA-256 `9c710bb285eff7ffb52c1608a2e8497451dd86bbd4057ddb444c04d4fcc415a0`: 79 explicit POM/JAR payloads and their four sidecars, 395 ordered Central HTTPS URLs. It validates coordinate paths, duplicates, destinations, statuses and caps after checking the raw manifest hash. It performs no mediation, recursive fetch, extraction, cache installation, class loading or acquired-code execution. The original fifteen-URL getter remains separate and unchanged.

Bodies stream into exclusive private nested `.partial` files under a fresh canonical operator-owned output. Per-file limits are 2 MiB/POM, 16 MiB/JAR and 64 KiB/sidecar; the aggregate body limit is 128 MiB. Every response has at most 64 header pairs and 16 KiB of UTF-8 key/value/separator/CRLF metadata. A dedicated request timer bounds connection/body work at 60 seconds; the root launcher owns the separate 900/1020-second process/scope limits and proof-bound cleanup.

The fixed 96-MiB metadata/log profile allocates 95 MiB to the getter, including its existing scope proof, response records and final receipt. Ordinary metadata writes retain a 1-MiB final-failure reserve. If a full receipt cannot fit, a small explicit `FAIL_METADATA_LIMIT` receipt preserves the bounded failed response and references the retained prior files; it cannot produce success. Root separately bounds child output plus controller records within the remaining 1 MiB. Specification and manifest framing are capped at 256 KiB before loading.

All served SHA-512/SHA-256/SHA-1 sidecars are checked; a bad strong checksum cannot fall back to a good legacy one. Missing sidecars remain visible, and same-origin hashes establish consistency only. Signatures remain unverified. TLS/status/checksum/path/size/time failures preserve the attempt and partial evidence without raising caps or retrying another coordinate.

The fake-response suite retains all eighteen original control obligations and adds fixed-manifest, coherent duplicate, coordinate, nested-path, aggregate and metadata-reserve controls. Run `python3 -m unittest discover -s porting/rust-parity-evidence/C01/batch33-passive-closure/tests -v` with an existing canonical `SYSON_BOOTSTRAP_TEST_ROOT`; local roots must remain under `/workspace/build/builderbob`, while GitHub-only fixtures may use canonical `RUNNER_TEMP`. Source/specification peer review and root execution remain pending; passive acquisition grants no JVM/JNI/plugin trust, mediated closure or full C01/RR16 acceptance.
